      title: 'Hanbok',
      desc: "Hanbok is Korea's traditional clothing, shaped over a long history. Early forms can already be seen in Goguryeo tomb murals and Silla clay figurines, and by the Three Kingdoms period the basic structure of today's hanbok — jeogori (jacket) with chima (skirt) or baji (pants) — had taken shape. It is made loose rather than fitted, so it is comfortable to wear, and its blend of straight and curved lines gives it a neat, elegant silhouette. Fabric and color once varied by social class, season, and occasion; today hanbok is mostly worn on holidays and formal ceremonies. Recently, \"saenghwal hanbok\" and \"gaeryang hanbok\" — traditional styles updated for everyday practicality — have become popular among younger generations, and the K-pop and K-drama wave has drawn international attention to hanbok as a symbol of Korean beauty.",
